A model's fully-qualified ID is in the form of <providerID>/<modelID>.
{{range .Footer.KeysSentence}}{{.}}
{{end}}

For per-model detail, use the 'info' command with a model's fully-qualified ID.

Examples:
{{range .Footer.Examples.Keys}}        bild info {{.}}
{{end}}
To search for providers or models, use the 'search' command followed by a
keyword, which matches against any slash-delimited token within a provider,
model, or alias that begins with that term.

{{range .Footer.MatchSentence}}{{.}}
{{end}}
Examples:
        bild search {{.Footer.Examples.Keyword}}
        bild search {{.ID}}

For more advanced searches, you may use regular expressions (RE2 syntax):

Example:
        bild search -r '{{.Footer.Examples.Alternation}}'

The -r option also allows searching for any part of a provider or model name,
not just the beginning:

Example:
        bild search -r {{.Footer.AnyPartArgument}}

It also allows searching across tokens:

Example:
        bild search -r '{{.Footer.Examples.AcrossTokens}}'
